 :root-cause
 "The generated routing-certificate resource gate used only five per-size warmups and ran after two ClojureScript compiler builds in the same JVM. A clean HotSpot process could therefore measure tiered-compilation or compiler/GC state rather than steady-state routing work. The CI expression threw before printing the failed result, hiding which resource dimension crossed its unchanged ceiling."
 :fix
 "Run the routing gate first in the fresh 1 GiB generated-resource JVM, use 40 deterministic warmups and 11 samples per size, and print the complete observation before a failed result throws. The exact P+2V+E logical checks and all allocation/latency ceilings remain unchanged."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.characterization-fixture-test/formal-ci-isolates-and-stops-performance-nrepls-test"
  "eacl.formal.routing-certificate-benchmark/run-gate!"
  ".github/workflows/formal.yml/Gate routing-certificate logical work and JVM allocation"
  "formal/verification/performance-gates.edn"]}
